From 29b321f6630d5b0ff60a87ddc7e97e76613d34cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 05:11:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 250/250] hir_typeck: no deref-target offer when `&&_` coerces
 to `&dyn Trait`

email_address 0.2.9 (tombi 1.8.4), lib.rs:679, the Deserialize visitor's
`visit_str`:

    <null> BUG: src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp:7099: TODO: check_ivar_poss - No none of the bounded types (OsStr, Path, str, [u8]) fit other bounds

    Error::invalid_value(Unexpected::Str(s), &exp.as_ref())

`exp` is a String, so `&exp.as_ref()` is `&&_` with `_` bounded by the
four `String: AsRef<_>` impls, passed where `&dyn Expected` is expected.
rustc unsizes before it autoderefs: `&_: Unsize<dyn Expected>`, i.e.
`&_: Expected`, holds for `_ = str` (serde's `impl Expected for &str`)
and for nothing else in the set. check_unsize_tys' deref-coercion
speculation, walking `&_` down to `_`, offered the destination itself
(`_ := dyn Expected`, the `&&dyn` deref route) as an UnsizeTo
possibility. check_ivar_poss__fails_bounds then accepted `str` through
the real coercion rule but vetoed it through that possibility
(`str: Expected` does not hold), as it rightly did the other three, and
the TODO fired.

When the ivar pairs with the destination itself and that destination is
a trait object, no offer is made: any `_` with an impl on the reference
is valid there, so the deref target is not a usable constraint. Offers
for dereferenced destinations (`Box<_>` to `Box<dyn Trait>`) are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---

diff --git a/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp b/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp
index 075a871a..5fe6a1f5 100644
--- a/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp
+++ b/src/hir_typeck/expr_cs.cpp
@@ -4466,6 +4466,17 @@ namespace {
                                 DEBUG("Destination level is an ivar, no deref target to offer");
                                 d_ty_p = nullptr;
                             }
+                            // A trait object destination paired with the ivar itself: rustc unsizes the source before
+                            // it autoderefs (`&_: Trait` for `&&_` to `&dyn Trait`), so any `_` with an impl on the
+                            // reference is valid and `_ == dyn Trait` (the deref route) is not a usable constraint.
+                            // email_address 0.2.9 lib.rs:679 (tombi 1.8.4) `&exp.as_ref()` as `&dyn Expected`: the
+                            // `String: AsRef<_>` candidate `str` passed the coercion rule (`&str: Expected`) but this
+                            // offer vetoed it (`str: Expected` does not hold) - "No none of the bounded types fit".
+                            if( d_ty_p && dst_derefs == 0 && context.m_ivars.get_type(*d_ty_p).data().is_TraitObject() )
+                            {
+                                DEBUG("Destination is a trait object the source may unsize to itself, no deref target to offer");
+                                d_ty_p = nullptr;
+                            }
                             if( d_ty_p )
                             {
                                 // TODO: This should be a `DerefTo` (can't do other unsizings?)
